

Summary of patch series in this merge:

- The 2 patch series "ocfs2/dlm: bound peer-controlled lengths in the
  o2dlm" (ea5b5609305a) from Bryam Vargas uses payload size verification
  to fix an issue where unbounded length and count fields in o2dlm receive
  handlers allow a malicious cluster node to crash or corrupt other nodes
  via out-of-bounds heap reads and writes.

- The 2 patch series "ocfs2: validate xattr entry bounds" from Cen Zhang
  validates OCFS2 xattr entry name/value bounds when xattr metadata is
  read and validated, before getxattr() or listxattr() can walk
  out-of-range entry arrays or offsets from corrupted metadata.

- The 2 patch series "taskstats: fix cgroupstats invalid fd handling and
  add selftests" from Yiyang Chen fixes an issue where cgroupstats
  mishandles invalid file descriptors and introduces a functional
  kselftest to prevent regressions.

- The 8 patch series "misc lib/raid/ improvements v2" from Christoph
  Hellwig improves the benchmark-based algorithm selection and adds kunit
  benchmarks for both the XOR and raid6 libraries, and tidies up a few
  very minor other bits.

- The 3 patch series "ocfs2: cluster: o2hb_region_pin() fixes" from
  Joseph Qi fixes three related issues in o2hb_region_pin().

- The 2 patch series "lib/ucs2_string.c: fix out-of-bounds read in
  ucs2_strnlen()" from Vincent Mailhol does that thing.

- The 2 patch series "ocfs2: harden heartbeat teardown races" from Cen
  Zhang fixes two OCFS2 heartbeat/o2net teardown races found by KASAN.

- The 2 patch series "taskstats: tidy up the cpumask command path" from
  Bradley Morgan provides two small cleanups in kernel/taskstats.c.

- The 2 patch series "ocfs2: validate active orphan slots during inode
  read" from ZhengYuan Huang makes the orphan slot handling more robust
  against corrupted filesystem images.

- The 2 patch series "ocfs2: bound-check both readdir re-validation
  scans" from Zhan Xusheng fixes another corrupted fs image issue.

